      "support_status": "SUFFICIENT",
      "rationale": "P020 explicitly attributes this possible contribution to repeated comparable observations."
    }
  },
  "signal_basis": {
    "component_id": "C038.signal_basis",
    "value": "Comparable booking observations locate delays by stage. A candidate stage recurs on multiple booking days in each investigation week and accounts for the greatest documented delay burden in both weeks. This pattern informs selection of a feasible change aimed at that stage, provided missing records cannot reverse the ranking and bookings suffice to apply the rule.",
    "scope": "A prospective, two-week practical trial-selection signal, assessed across comparable equipment and crew groups; it provides neither statistical proof nor causal identification.",
